      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Chronic pelvic pains are one of the most frequent complaints in our daily gynecological practice, motivating at least a quarter of our consultants. As it usually puts the practitioner ill at ease in a difficult situation, we will try to understand the meaning of those particular pains, thus defined: a duration outlasting 6 months and the absence or the ineffective suppression of any organic--somatic--substratum. But every alleged pain is real and true, and we must work on that. To validate such suffering, to accept such repetitive complaints, can also be a therapeutic medical approach, even if it is less gratifying for the gynecologist, and certainly less customary."},
